  <h1>Java Encapsulation</h1>

  <p>Encapsulation is the process of wrapping data (variables) and methods into a single unit (class).</p>
  <p>It helps protect the internal state of an object and only expose what’s necessary through methods (getters/setters).</p>

  <p><strong>Benefits of Encapsulation:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Improved code security</li>
    <li>Control over data (read/write access)</li>
    <li>Better modularity and code maintainability</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Simple Java Code:</strong></p>
  <pre><code>
class Person {
    private String name;

    public void setName(String n) {
        name = n;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Person p = new Person();
        p.setName("Aditya");
        System.out.println("Name: " + p.getName());
    }
}
  </code></pre>

